gradle-wrapper.jar
/.gradle
/captures/
/gradlew
/gradlew.bat
/local.properties
GeneratedPluginRegistrant.java
.cxx/

# Remember to never publicly share your keystore.
# See https://flutter.dev/to/reference-keystore
key.properties
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks

# ONE EXCEPTION, and it is deliberately spelled out in full rather than
# loosened above.
#
# app/preview-keystore.jks is the committed PREVIEW key. It has to be in the
# repository, because Android only installs an update over an existing app
# when both carry the same signature, and a key that lives on one machine
# cannot sign builds made on a CI runner. build.gradle.kts explains the whole
# reasoning where the config lives.
#
# The ban above stays exactly as it is. It is what stops a REAL Play upload
# key, or a key.properties holding real passwords, from being committed by
# somebody in a hurry, and that ban is worth more than the small awkwardness
# of naming the one file that is allowed through. Never widen this to a
# pattern: a second .jks appearing here unannounced is the thing to catch.
!app/preview-keystore.jks
